00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.439
associated with the Kremlin.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.140
It says that since

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.408
the start of the invasion,

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.877
Vladimir Putin has for the most part,

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.679
stopped using his private airplane.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:13.513
You see it there, right?

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.247
He used to do it.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:14.481
You know,

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.482
the whole warhead of state

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:16.716
walked down the stairs.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.217
No.

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:20.153
Now, this is his preferred mode

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.354
of transportation,

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.622
according to the dossier group,

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.623
which is run by Mikhail

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.592
Khodorkovsky, an opposition leader.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:26.793
Putin is traveling mostly

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.261
in this armored train

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:28.628
equipped

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:31.164
with a special communication system.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.432
Why the train?

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:33.299
Well, earlier

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.335
I spoke to Ilya Roaster Svenska,

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.003
a reporter with the Dossier Center,

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.304
and he told me that the

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.706
Russian president is afraid

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:42.976
the psychological

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.811
reason of using this train

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.579
is that he's scared.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.948
He's scared that he can be tracked.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:50.817
That his plane can be tracked

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.453
and that his plane can be shut down

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.289
by NATO air forces

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:59.359
or by the air forces of Ukraine.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:01.494
A wise missile,

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:02.562
some kind of a missile

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.264
that he's Ukrainian, British

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.533
or anything like this can happen.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:07.767
So he's scared

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.202
and he believes that it is

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.036
a more secure

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.371
way to travel,

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:14.040
that nobody will know where he is going

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.041
and nobody will understand

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:17.811
that he's inside the stream.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.313
No one will know because Roger Penske

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:21.514
says it looks like

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.849
a normal passenger train

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:24.317
that gray with the red stripe.

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.586
That's the Russian passenger train.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.921
Make no mistake, though,

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.656
this particular train

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:31.024
is not like the others

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.462
There are like three locomotives.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:38.064
Putin's train has three of them

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:40.467
because it's really heavy.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:41.434
It's armor.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.769
And so it's hairy

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.637
and it needs more locomotives.

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:45.271
This train,

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.640
it has some kind of special equipment

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.209
for special communications.

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:51.811
He wants to communicate securely.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.647
He needs some special lines to

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:55.882
to communicate

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.383
with his prime minister

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.918
and other officials

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.920
and to be sure that he's not listened

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.789
by some foreign intelligence.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.125
And he can see part of this part

00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.192
of this equipment

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.695
on the roof, off of the cars.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.631
You can see part of it from the roof

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:12.932
and it's heavy, it's armored.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.000
So it takes three

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.235
locomotives to transport it,

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:15.869
not just one.

00:02:15.869 --> 00:02:17.370
General Hertling, in this context,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.305
because as Steve mentioned,

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.206
Khodorkovsky in

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:20.807
is his group,

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:21.541
the dossier group,

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:22.442
that has done all this.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.043
This research is painstaking research

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:26.179
